00:07:50.453 --> 00:07:51.990
- oh my God dear.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:53.460
- In terms of how long it took.

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:58.460
So for Craig, it was obviously
a much longer journey.

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:00.300
I mean, by the time I met him,

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:03.540
he'd been diving every day for
six or seven years already.

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:06.090
The octopus had died already.

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:11.090
And what that meant was there
was an awful lot of footage.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:16.580
So the first three months was
just looking at what we had

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:18.900
so that we could start to figure out

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:21.453
exactly where our story was gonna focus.

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:27.033
And then it was three years of editing.

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:29.033
- So it was.

00:08:29.033 --> 00:08:31.680
- I imagine, so that's why I
started off with this question

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:35.463
because it has to have been a
gargantuan job of getting it,

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:38.550
but it's beautifully done.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:42.840
It looks so gorgeous on a
large screen and very moving.

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:45.360
I don't know, somehow
it felt much more moving

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:47.250
on the large screen.

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:49.173
I had to hold back tears as well.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:55.110
But I would like to open it up

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:56.850
to questions from the audience.

